presentations. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations. ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "zany ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "eccentric; unconventional; unusual", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Aunt Nelly can be a bit zany at times. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le01ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about family.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Superlatives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use a superlative adjective to express the highest degree of a quality. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use a superlative adjective to talk about one thing or person in a group of things. You always use <span class=\"strong\"> the </span> with the superlative. <br>Superlatives can be regular or irregular. The structure of the regular superlative is:  <br> the + adjective-est <Br>  or <br>    the most adjective", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjective\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Superlative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Regular\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"fine <br>quiet <br>small <br>different <br>intelligent\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the finest <br>the quietest <br>the smallest <Br>the most different <br>the most <br>intelligent\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Irregular\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"good <br>bad\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the best <br>the worst\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "This is the best coffee!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She is the most intelligent person in the family.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The MOMA houses some of the finest art in the world.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Rainy weather is the worst.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Habits and Routines", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you talk about someone's habits and routines, you use the Simple Present tense and frequency words.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use expressions of frequency to say how many times you do an activity. <br> This can be an adverb like<span class=\"italic\"> often, sometimes</span>   or <span class=\"italic\">never</span>. It can also be expression like <span class=\"italic\">a lot, all the time</span> or <span class=\"italic\">when I can</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adverbs\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Expressions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"always\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"every day/week/month\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"usually\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"most of the time\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"often\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"every other day/week/month\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sometimes\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"once in a while\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"occasionally\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"from time to time\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"hardly ever\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"when ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"never\\\"}\",\"\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I always have black coffee in the morning.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "My house was hardly ever noisy. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I go to the movies once in a while.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "My brother works every other day.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "My teacher occasionally asks to check out homework.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to knit", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to use long needles to make a sweater or scarf", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Do you know how to knit?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le01ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to weave", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make fabric on a loom", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I want to learn how to weave next year. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le01ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "niece", "type": "name"}, {"content": "my sister or brother's daughter ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My sister's daughter, my niece Alison, is 2 today.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le01ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "nephew", "type": "name"}, {"content": "my sister or brother's son", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My sister's son, my nephew Greg, is at university now.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le01ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to run ragged", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to keep someone very busy", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My sister's children run her ragged! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le01ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "bookish ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "always reading a book ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My family are all bookish. They are always reading something! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le01ob01aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "black sheep ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the rebel of the family; different from the others", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I am the black sheep of my family. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le01ob01aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "grumpy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "cranky; irritable", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He's always grumpy when he's hungry or tired. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le01ob01aud09", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"content": "engenn6le01ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Find adjective to describe some people you know or admire.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use the adjective in the superlative form.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Say what actions the people do to make you see them this way.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write 70 to 90 words.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your sentence aloud to a partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I look up and use adjectives.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use the superlative.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about people I know or admire.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my sentences aloud.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn6le01ob01re2img05.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn6le01ob01re2img05.jpg", "time": "1", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Ah \u2026 this is the best coffee with the smallest hint of cinnamon! I always have black coffee in the morning. I missed the coffee here. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I often drink tea ... you know that's the finest of British traditions. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: How is your family by the way? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Aunt Nelly is good, zany as ever. She's in a creative phase knitting and weaving.<br>"}, {"image": "engenn6le01ob01re2img01.jpg", "time": "26000", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Does she usually do crafts? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: She does from time to time.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: My sister sews once in a while. My niece and nephew are loud and usually run her ragged. She adores them.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: My house was hardly ever noisy. Mum, Dad and Teddy are all bookish and the quietest people I know. I'm the black sheep.<br>"}, {"image": "engenn6le01ob01re2img06.jpg", "time": "51000", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Black what?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Black sheep. The most different from the others. What about your family?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Mom is the sweetest person. She never gets upset or angry. I see her whenever I can. Dad is a bit grumpy once in a while. They both come from larger families so I have lots of cousins.<br>"}], "audiosrc": "engenn6le01ob01re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn6le01ob01re2img05.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can talk about family life.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about people's habits.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can use superlatives.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Who are the quietest, the brightest,  or the most interesting people you know?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Why do you think that?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "He is the most interesting person!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " Vanessa talks about her <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">mum</span> and dad and brother, Teddy", "type": "text"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": [{"content": "The British use the word <span class=\"italic\">\"mum\"</span> for mother. North Americans gener